# Written and deleted by `pnpm typecheck:infra-pure`. Present only if that
# script was interrupted.
.tsconfig.infra-pure.json

# Written and removed by `apps/api/test/tenant-from-input.test.ts`, which lints
# fixtures at real paths so the P0-48 rule is tested the way it runs — the
# configuration keys on the directory, so it has to be a directory we ship. The
# cleanup is a `finally`, which a killed test process never reaches, and the
# suite sweeps strays on the way in and out. This is the third net: an
# interrupted run leaves one in `src/`, where `pnpm lint` fails on the `any`
# inside it for a reason nobody would trace back to a test.
*.fixture.ts
